    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a new owner matches an existing owner's household (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace):\n- If `sharesHousehold` is not `true` \u2192 still rejected with `409` (existing behavior, preserved).\n- If `sharesHousehold` is `true` \u2192 the owner is allowed, and a stable `householdId` is assigned to the new owner **and** back-filled onto the existing household member(s). The `householdId` is returned on the owner.\n\n**Design choice \u2014 stable identifier:** `householdId` is derived deterministically from the normalized last name + address (`UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes(...)`), so every member of a household maps to the same value regardless of creation order, satisfying the \"stable shared identifier\" requirement.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 reworked the household duplicate check to collect matching members, assign/back-fill the shared `householdId` when opting in, set it on the new owner, and added the `householdId(...)` helper + imports.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only string property on the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it; `sharesHousehold` already existed as write-only on `OwnerFields`).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` (two joiners get an equal, non-blank `householdId`) passes.",
